From: mtk23510 <mtk23510@mediatek.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: FT MIC: revert unconditional need_ml_rsn=1 in MLE
 branch

mtk-hostapd-0611r-010-roaming_ft_mic_fix.patch made three changes:
  A) RX branch: force need_ml_rsn=1 instead of gating on
     ml_info.bss_para_change_cnt_present.
  B) TX branch: force need_ml_rsn=1 instead of gating on
     ml_group->ml_link_num > 1.
  C) RSNXE append loop: skip per-link RSNXE when caller passed rsnxe=NULL
     (i.e. when STA did not include RSNXE on air).

C is the change that actually fixed the previous MLO FT-802.1X regression
where the AP injected zeroed per-link RSNXE bytes into the Reassoc Resp
FTE MIC -> STA MIC validation failed -> STA emitted PMF Deauth.

A and B were over-corrections. With A in effect, every Reassoc Req that
carries a Basic ML element now triggers the per-link RSNE MIC recipe on
RX, even for STAs whose MLE does not signal bss_para_change_cnt and that
do not include per-link RSNE bytes in their own MIC input. The result is
hostapd printing "FT: Invalid MIC in FTIE" and answering every Reassoc
Req with status 55 (INVALID_FTIE), in a tight loop.

This patch:
  - Reverts A back to the original gate on ml_info.bss_para_change_cnt_present.
  - Reverts B back to the original gate on ml_group->ml_link_num > 1.
  - Keeps C (need_ml_rsn && rsnxe) intact so the previous PMF-Deauth
    regression does not return.

Signed-off-by: mtk23510 <mtk23510@mediatek.com>
---
 src/common/wpa_common.c | 12 ++++--------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

--- a/src/common/wpa_common.c
+++ b/src/common/wpa_common.c
@@ -1023,11 +1023,9 @@
 #endif
 				}

-				/* MLE present in this Reassoc Req -> use per-link
-				 * RSNE path on RX. Must match TX so STA's MIC
-				 * validates.
-				 */
-				need_ml_rsn = 1;
+				/* fourth message, no need to add legacy rsn */
+				if (ml_info.bss_para_change_cnt_present)
+					need_ml_rsn = 1;

 				wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "FT: MLO valid links=%x, need_ml_rsn=%u",
 					valid_links, need_ml_rsn);
@@ -1065,11 +1063,9 @@
 					}
 				}

-				/* MLE will be present in this Reassoc Resp -> use
-				 * per-link RSNE path on TX. Must match RX so the
-				 * STA's MIC validates.
-				 */
-				need_ml_rsn = 1;
+				/* MLO: per-link RSNE recipe only when truly multi-link */
+				if (ml_group->ml_link_num > 1)
+					need_ml_rsn = 1;

 				if (need_ml_rsn) {
 					for (i = 0; i < MAX_NUM_MLO_LINKS; i++) {
